Task Monki receives records whose ordinal is unique and increasing only within a run; records from runs may interleave. A provider-completed record is telemetry, report-verified is local completion evidence, and the required final rule for the active run is: report-verified => completed; otherwise process-exit => interrupted; otherwise running, independent of record arrival order. Consider:

type E = { runId: string; ordinal: number; kind: 'provider-completed'|'process-exit'|'report-verified' };
function project(active: string, journal: E[]) {
  let lastOrdinal = 0, providerDone = false;
  let status: 'running'|'interrupted'|'completed' = 'running';
  for (const e of journal) {
    if (e.ordinal <= lastOrdinal) continue;
    lastOrdinal = e.ordinal;
    if (e.runId !== active) continue;
    if (e.kind === 'provider-completed') providerDone = true;
    else if (e.kind === 'process-exit' && !providerDone) status = 'interrupted';
    else if (e.kind === 'report-verified' && status === 'running') status = 'completed';
  }
  return status;
}

For active Y, trace A is X/40 exit, Y/1 provider-completed, Y/2 exit, Y/3 report-verified. Trace B is Y/1 provider-completed, Y/2 exit. Trace C is Y/1 exit, Y/2 report-verified. Give the current outputs, required outputs, all independent root causes, and the smallest invariant-preserving repair.
